THE CROSS-CHECK: every R_* leg must leave rldimi at 27/27 and every D_* leg must leave rlwimi at 28/28.  A
failure there means the mutators touched shared code, or a probe is sensitive to the other instruction.

CHECKS: SIBLING PARITY -- the two sibling handlers now each have a promoted detector; rldicl (#522) is the third
sibling and is gated separately (exempt, lacks the protocol).  CLAIM -> ROW / GUARD-BODY -- unchanged from
table 1 (its PRETABLE.out in each row's killtable_20260911/).  CHANNEL -- every row reads a register value.
